# they write artifacts relative to the cwd — so running one from the repo root
# was about to be committed with `git add -A`.

# One-off ops/probe scripts. Several build a LayeredBackend against a LIVE
# profile database (see .claude/repair_step1.py, profile-b.db) — the
# exact pattern docs/e2e-execution.md forbids and the 0.8.20 changelog names
# as a cause of two data-loss incidents. Committed, they are standing
# instructions a future session might run. Scoped to scripts so shared
# .claude config (agents, settings) can still be tracked deliberately.
# 2026-08-26 external sweep, N2.
.claude/*.py

# A SQLite URI used as a filename. `sqlite3 "file:$DB?mode=ro" ...` creates a
# real file under that literal name when URI handling is off, and `*.db` does
# not match it because the name ends in `?mode=ro`. One such file — 265 rows of
# real memory content — was committed and pushed on 2026-08-27.
# T590 is the check that does not depend on the name at all.
file:*
*mode=ro*
